# Roles associated with requirements in ML-enabled systems — results

**Question.** Which two roles have the highest proportion of association with requirements?

## Data / cleaning (traceability)
- File `data/requirements_engineering_for_ML-enabled_systems.csv`: 276 respondents × 202 columns.
- Sentinels → NA: `-77`/`-66` (item not answered) and `-99` (NA in numeric / free-text fields): 18,637 cells.
- `"0"` → NA **only** in label-coded categoricals (D4_Role, Q1/Q2 relevance & difficulty, D11, Q6/Q7): 312 cells. Genuine 0 kept in D5–D8 counts and Q3 effort.
- `I don't know` excluded from denominators (46 cells in Q1+Q2). Q8 contains no "I don't know".
- Q8 block (`Q8_ML_Addressing_*`) is **dichotomous** (`quoted` / `not quoted`), not Likert → "association present" = `quoted`.
- 82 respondents never answered Q8 (all with Status = Suspended) → **main denominator N = 194** (all 8 items complete per item).
- D4_Role: 23 missing; 62 "Other, which one?" free texts → regex map: 32 mapped, 30 unmapped (17 academic/research-type, 13 other).

## Main analysis (Option A)
p_r = % of the 194 Q8 respondents answering `quoted` for that role. Bootstrap over respondents,
B = 10,000, seed = 42, percentile 2.5/97.5. Others excluded from ranking.

| rank | role | quoted / N | % | 95% CI |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Project Lead / Project Manager | 99/194 | 51.03 | [43.81, 58.25] |
| 2 | Data Scientist | 95/194 | 48.97 | [41.75, 56.19] |
| 3 | Business Analyst | 50/194 | 25.77 | [19.59, 31.96] |
| 4 | Developer | 37/194 | 19.07 | [13.92, 24.74] |
| 5 | Solution Architect | 24/194 | 12.37 | [7.73, 17.01] |
| 6 | Requirements Engineer | 20/194 | 10.31 | [6.19, 14.43] |
| 7 | Tester | 2/194 | 1.03 | [0.00, 2.58] |

**Paired PL vs DS (same respondents).** difference = +2.06 pp, bootstrap 95% CI [−7.73, +11.34];
P(PL>DS) = 0.644; exact McNemar on discordant pairs (47 vs 43) p = 0.752. → the **set** {PL, DS} is the
top-2 in 100% of bootstrap replicates (Business Analyst never enters top-2: 0%), but the **1st/2nd order is
not resolvable** (DS ranked first in 31.7% of replicates; stable across seeds 1/7/42/2024/31337).

