S4 corroboration — Q1 importance of "Problem Understanding & Requirements": 175/184 (95.1%, CI [91.85, 97.83])
rated High/Extremely Relevant (excluding 1 "I don't know" and 91 NA) → requirements are seen as decisive, which is
consistent with roles being judged by *perceived* ownership rather than by title.

## Documented discrepancy (not a result)
Cited 49.6% (CI [49.219, 49.981]) and 61.389% (CI [60.955, 61.822]) are **not reproducible** from this export:
- CI half-width ≈0.4 pp implies effective n ≈ 48,000–66,000 (vs 194/276 respondents); with N=194 the CI is ≈±7 pp.
- 61.389% requires a fraction with N a multiple of 360 (e.g. 221/360); no k/N with N ≤ 276 equals it.
  49.6% requires N multiple of 125 (62/125, 124/250). Closest with N=194: 96/194 = 49.485; 119/194 = 61.340.
- Closest candidates found: Data Scientist 48.97% (49.47% completed-only) ≈ 49.6%; Project Lead with Others
  mapped 60.31% (or BA∪DS 63.40%) ≈ 61.389%.
- Hypothesis: figures come from a different/extended export (larger sample) or a mis-scaled CI; per researcher
  instruction no grid-search was fitted to "match" them.

## Limitations
Q8 dichotomised (no Likert threshold recoverable); item-non-response concentrated in suspended participants;
n = 2 for Tester/Requirements Engineer (unstable); heuristic Others mapping (30 unmapped); self-reported
perception, not organisational audit; cross-sectional single-respondent-per-organisation.
